# Deploying apex-frontend

This repo is a **static Vite SPA**. Production API calls go to the **Fastify backend** (`apex` package), configured via `VITE_API_URL` at build time—not to routes inside this frontend repo.

## Vercel (primary)

- **Root directory:** `apex-frontend` when the git root is the monorepo; otherwise project root is this folder.
- **Build command:** `pnpm build` (or `npm run build`)
- **Install command:** `pnpm install`
- **Output directory:** `dist`
- **Environment:** set `VITE_API_URL` to the production API base URL (no trailing slash) for Production and Preview.
- **`vercel.json`** at repo root defines SPA rewrites and `no-store` cache headers for `index.html`.

Use Vercel MCP tools when available. You may run `pnpm build` locally to verify; deployment does not require a Node server from this package.

## Netlify

Not configured in this repo (no `netlify.toml`). Do not assume Netlify functions or `dist/spa` paths from the old Fusion starter.

## Preview vs production

- Open Preview / `pnpm dev` is for UI review only—not a substitute for setting `VITE_API_URL` on the deployed build.
- After deploy, smoke-test login, feed, and one authenticated API screen against the real backend.

## Do not

- Deploy expecting `pnpm start` or `dist/server`—those were removed with the Fusion boilerplate.
- Point `VITE_API_URL` at the Vercel frontend URL; API requests must hit the Fastify host.
